    Cold conserves r(M_i + law mass) with the law's term in both states, share mass: cold at outer third over Newtonian contraction, psi with it, psi Newtonian: canonical 60-100 x0.96 psi 0.54 (was 0.48); canonical 150-200 x0.94 psi 0.31 (was 0.29); canonical 200-250 x0.96 psi 0.50 (was 0.44); alt 60-100 x0.96 psi 0.47 (was 0.47); alt 150-200 x0.95 psi 0.33 (was 0.32); alt 200-250 x0.96 psi 0.41 (was 0.36). Removes nothing; it only changes how far the cold falls.

[2 streaming velocity] CLOSED AT G1 | constants 0 | particle-like no
    30 km/s at z 1000 (PROVISIONAL): comoving drift 0.048 Mpc against Lagrangian radius by bin 0.39 0.62 0.94 1.53 1.99 2.26 Mpc: ratio 0.032 at 150-200, 0.078 at 60-100. Moves baryons relative to cold, removes none, larger for dwarfs. Short x23 even read as a removal fraction.

[3 GMC and cluster scattering] CLOSED AT G1 | constants 0 | particle-like no
    All gas in clumps of M_p, smeared over R_last, lnL 10, 13.8 Gyr (generous; PROVISIONAL clump mass): specific energy, (km/s)^2 / need V^2: 150-200 M_p 1e+06: 20 / 29481 = 0.00; 150-200 M_p 1e+07: 199 / 29481 = 0.01; 200-250 M_p 1e+07: 113 / 48334 = 0.00. Clump lives 10-30 Myr so x 0.3 duty at best is not applied; a clump of 1e7 is at the top end. Rises with gas, not V, and gas-rich dwarfs get it first.

[4 transient spirals] CLOSED AT G1 | constants 0 | particle-like no
    J budget: fraction of the disc's J the cold must absorb to pay lifting at corotation Omega_p = V/2.2 R_d, share / EM1: 150-200 1.06 / 1.85; 200-250 1.02 / 1.69. So about all of the disc's J or more, while observed discs keep most of theirs (retention near 0.6-1, PROVISIONAL): at most 0.4 of J can go, short x2.6 or more at perfect delivery. LC1 has no spirals; the exchange efficiency itself isn't computed, and it reaches cold only at resonances. Bars with stronger torque leave unbarred discs at the same miss (BT1), and spirals are not stronger than bars.

